WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:00.953
Instructor: Okay, so we saw

00:00.953 --> 00:02.910
that we can check out a particular commit

00:02.910 --> 00:04.620
using a commit hash,

00:04.620 --> 00:06.180
but there's another way in git

00:06.180 --> 00:08.040
that we can reference other commits.

00:08.040 --> 00:11.010
We can reference things based upon HEAD.

00:11.010 --> 00:12.906
The syntax is kind of, it's a little weird,

00:12.906 --> 00:14.580
but it looks like this:

00:14.580 --> 00:16.470
HEAD, and then a tilde,

00:16.470 --> 00:18.510
which is usually above the tab key

00:18.510 --> 00:19.980
and then a number.

00:19.980 --> 00:23.070
So HEAD, tilde one, is actually going to refer

00:23.070 --> 00:25.980
to whatever commit comes before HEAD.

00:25.980 --> 00:27.900
Think of it as HEAD minus one.

00:27.900 --> 00:29.070
HEAD tilde two,

00:29.070 --> 00:31.770
it's whatever comes two commits before HEAD,

00:31.770 --> 00:33.900
the grandparent commit.

00:33.900 --> 00:35.670
So if this is where HEAD is,

00:35.670 --> 00:38.190
if I check out HEAD tilde one,

00:38.190 --> 00:39.840
it's the previous commit.

00:39.840 --> 00:43.560
HEAD tilde two, it's this commit, three is this one.

00:43.560 --> 00:45.180
So I don't use this all that often,

00:45.180 --> 00:48.113
but sometimes, if you have a reason to reference

00:48.113 --> 00:50.850
what you did in the last commit

00:50.850 --> 00:53.310
and you don't want to go look up that commit hash,

00:53.310 --> 00:57.240
you can still very easily reference it with HEAD tilde one.

00:57.240 --> 00:59.490
So I'll show that very quickly.

00:59.490 --> 01:00.720
On our master branch,

01:00.720 --> 01:01.953
let's just take a look.

01:03.990 --> 01:05.940
So we've got begin chapter three,

01:05.940 --> 01:07.350
that's where we are right now.

01:07.350 --> 01:09.390
If I just wanna go back one commit,

01:09.390 --> 01:12.090
I could copy this, right?

01:12.090 --> 01:13.680
And then check that out

01:13.680 --> 01:14.910
or, I can do this.

01:14.910 --> 01:19.910
Git checkout HEAD tilde one, not 21, just one.

01:22.050 --> 01:24.540
And once again we're back to detached HEAD,

01:24.540 --> 01:26.790
because we checked out a particular commit.

01:26.790 --> 01:29.375
This is just a different way to reference that commit,

01:29.375 --> 01:31.680
we just said the previous commit,

01:31.680 --> 01:32.700
but it's still a commit.

01:32.700 --> 01:33.960
We're not on a branch.

01:33.960 --> 01:35.220
And we see that here:

01:35.220 --> 01:37.620
HEAD is now pointing to this commit:

01:37.620 --> 01:39.690
add headings to all files.

01:39.690 --> 01:42.570
So before, HEAD was pointing to master,

01:42.570 --> 01:44.280
which is still pointing to this commit.

01:44.280 --> 01:45.930
Now HEAD is one before

01:45.930 --> 01:48.840
and what we see in our file,

01:48.840 --> 01:50.040
we probably won't notice a whole lot,

01:50.040 --> 01:51.600
but there's no chapter three.

01:51.600 --> 01:52.890
That is the difference.

01:52.890 --> 01:54.600
Chapter one and chapter two are here,

01:54.600 --> 01:57.840
but chapter three was the next commit.

01:57.840 --> 02:00.120
It still exists on master of course.

02:00.120 --> 02:03.360
So from here, if I wanna go back one commit again,

02:03.360 --> 02:05.220
I can just do the same command:

02:05.220 --> 02:08.070
get checkout HEAD minus, or tilde, one;

02:08.070 --> 02:10.320
because HEAD is now right here,

02:10.320 --> 02:12.843
I can still reference one commit prior.

02:14.100 --> 02:18.330
Okay, and now we go back one, one further.

02:18.330 --> 02:20.163
So there we are, HEAD is now here.

02:21.060 --> 02:21.893
And we can see,

02:21.893 --> 02:24.153
we don't have those headings in my files anymore.

02:24.990 --> 02:27.090
Chapter two, chapter one,

02:27.090 --> 02:29.490
they used to have a heading up top.

02:29.490 --> 02:31.020
And that's kind of all I want to show.

02:31.020 --> 02:33.450
Of course, I'll switch back to master now.

02:33.450 --> 02:34.953
Git switch master.

02:36.630 --> 02:38.040
And now we have those headings back

02:38.040 --> 02:40.260
and we have chapter three back.

02:40.260 --> 02:43.560
So we're back up to date with the master branch reference.

02:43.560 --> 02:45.660
One other thing that we can do,

02:45.660 --> 02:48.690
to get back to the branch we were on.

02:48.690 --> 02:51.120
So, lemme try and explain that in a better way.

02:51.120 --> 02:53.430
If I check out some commit,

02:53.430 --> 02:54.900
I go into detached HEAD.

02:54.900 --> 02:56.640
Right now I'm on master, right?

02:56.640 --> 03:00.120
So if I check out HEAD tilde, I don't know.

03:00.120 --> 03:01.773
Let's go way back, like eight.

03:03.210 --> 03:04.800
We're way back here.

03:04.800 --> 03:06.090
This commit here.

03:06.090 --> 03:08.850
Okay, now if I wanna go back to where I was,

03:08.850 --> 03:10.440
I wanna leave detached HEAD.

03:10.440 --> 03:11.910
One option is to just remember

03:11.910 --> 03:14.430
what branch I was on, Master,

03:14.430 --> 03:16.740
and go back to Master, git switch Master.

03:16.740 --> 03:19.530
The other option is git switch with a dash

03:19.530 --> 03:21.060
and that will just take me back

03:21.060 --> 03:23.580
to whatever branch I was on last.

03:23.580 --> 03:25.950
And that happens to be master,

03:25.950 --> 03:27.540
but I could show a different example,

03:27.540 --> 03:30.330
we have this other branch,

03:30.330 --> 03:31.410
I already forgot the name.

03:31.410 --> 03:32.243
What is it?

03:32.243 --> 03:33.720
Chapter two, redo.

03:33.720 --> 03:36.483
If we check that out or switch to it, either one,

03:37.440 --> 03:38.820
okay, that's where I was.

03:38.820 --> 03:41.970
Now I'm gonna go back, git checkout HEAD,

03:41.970 --> 03:44.940
let's do tilde one.

03:44.940 --> 03:46.590
Okay, so I'm on this branch.

03:46.590 --> 03:48.400
I'm gonna go back one commit

03:50.760 --> 03:53.340
and now I just wanna leave detached HEAD.

03:53.340 --> 03:54.690
I don't remember what branch I was on,

03:54.690 --> 03:56.460
or I'm just lazy.

03:56.460 --> 03:58.080
I do git switch dash

03:58.080 --> 04:00.510
and it takes me back to where I left off.

04:00.510 --> 04:02.210
Okay, that's all I wanted to show.
